          "title": "Patterns and caveats",
          "body": "The operations that need a plan. Start a data migration with `makemigrations --empty`, then write a `RunPython` function that uses historical models. Keep schema and data changes in separate migrations when a backfill is large.",
          "code": "# Data migration with historical model\ndef forwards(apps, schema_editor):\n    Order = apps.get_model(\"shop\", \"Order\")\n    Order.objects.filter(status=\"\").update(status=\"pending\")\n\nclass Migration(migrations.Migration):\n    dependencies = [(\"shop\", \"0004_order_status\")]\n    operations = [migrations.RunPython(forwards, migrations.RunPython.noop)]\n\n# State/DB divergence\nmigrations.SeparateDatabaseAndState(\n    state_operations=[migrations.AddField(...)],\n    database_operations=[migrations.RunSQL(...)],\n)",
